 behind the  scenes too much talking but when the  action scenes are there they're great  and that is the general vibe I got off  this trailer so  part is good Scarlett Johansson looks to  be doing fine with the major as she's  written but I'll kind of come back to  that and I really like those sort of  kabuki looking makeup thing I like the  kind of came apart got spidery that was  a cool thing but the first things sort  of trick or might yeah I don't know  about that was seeing the major she took  off her cloak and she had the you know  the skin type flesh tone thing and that  was the first thing was like you should  have altered that more because in my  opinion at least the skin type flesh  don't think it worked in the anime it's  not working for me here and if they were  going to keep the skin type thing I wish  they hadn't have made it flesh tone and  that's one of a couple of things along  with the look of otto and his eyes that  i think just doesn't work as well in  live action yes you can translate it  accurately I think they have in both  cases with the look for the major in  that suit and with batos eyes but  looking at them unlike that's not  pleasing for me to look at it's not  working those are my first red flags the  other ones came up after as it was going  along and we started to get certain  things laid over in the voice-over now  before I dig into this i will add the  caveat that it is possible that this  trailer is not completely accurate that  there are overlaid lines that may not  even appear in the movie that they may  be putting you know they may be breaking  things down and oversimplify it for the  purposes of a trailer in order to get  butts in seats I accept that all that is  possible but I'm not going to judge my  opinion of this film based off what I  think is different about the trailer I'm  going to judge the trailer itself and  what they actually put in front of me  that's what they gave me that's what I'm  going to judge it at this point I'm  going to take them at their word that  this is an accurate representation of  the film so based on that first thing  that was said that made me go was when  the woman said to the major you're the  first of your kind I'm like wait what I  can't remember if that ever came up is  being part of her lore that like she was  one of the first full body sort of  things but even if she was she's not  unique at the time this story is taking  place she's not supposed to be that put  me on high alert and then once I was on  high alert I got really really unnerved  as the thing progressed and we got this  vibe of things said by the villain and  things said by the major that  puts her in this questioning phase now  she should be questioned but she should  be questioning grand philosophical ideas  what is a soul do I have one did I ever  have one did I lose it as I became more  and more physically mechanical do I  still retain that it can it be you know  can it move Kenneth transfer what is the  nature of beach she should be asking all  of this unfortunately the question she's  asking in this trailer are Who am I  where did I come from and that's really  boiling it down that's oversimplifying  that's basically turning the major into  Jason Bourne and I don't like that that  kind of got realized when the villain  went you know they didn't save you they  stole you or track you or whatever it is  he said basically implying that there's  some sort of conspiracy behind her  creation and like there's some part of  her history that she's not allowed to  remember and I don't care about any of  that I don't care about the majors past  I don't want a mystery of her past I  want to know her future I want to know  the trajectory that she's on I want to  know where the questions that she's  asking about the very nature of  existence are leading her in her  evolution as a character and as a  physical embodiment and as a mind that's  what I want I don't want to get hung up  on how she already got to where she is  now if you want to send the thing  further back and build up towards her  asking those big questions that's fine  that's about I actually thinking through  the franchisee building that would make  a lot more sense poor put her sort of  more in the state that she was in  standalone complex and then over time  bring her forward to where she's really  questioning the way she wasn't that  original 90s film but instead you really  I'm getting this conspiracy they're  hiding her pass from her vibe and that  is such a derivative oversimplification  of the questions that she is supposed to  be asking about herself and about the  world and I don't like that I don't like  it at all again I will cop to the  possibility that maybe it's only  oversimplified for the trail and I won't  be in the film but again I'm going to  what they gave me what they gave me is  oversimplified to a point that has me  really really really nervous so high  marks for the visuals overall accepting  the couple little things that I pointed  out but visually I think it's going to  be great I was never worried about the  visual presentation I was sure it was  gonna look great I think the director is  a very good visual storyteller but my  concerns from the very beginning I said  in the very first video I ever made  related to this when they first cast  Scarlett Johansson way way back before  everyone lost their mind over that fact  I said way back then that my concerns  are all about how they're going to  handle the story and those concerns are  not waylaid by this trailer at all in  fact it seems to be confirming a lot of  my fears so there's my thoughts on the  first full goes in the shell trailer  have you seen it what did you think  about it whatever you thought drop  something down in the comments and let's  talk about it don't forget to Like  subscribe check me out on Twitter at  council of geeks give a listen to the  council beats podcast available on  iTunes and stitcher and until next time  this council is adjourned

